  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2c339bd32a3c8c245bda86601cd991ec, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.AlreadyPressedBeat
  _note: 
  _inkMaterial: {fileID: 2100000, guid: 5556814e11032244ab3e6a5098e86fae, type: 2}
  _font: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 579a746deee295d4682ed64faa1cf59d, type: 2}
  _buttonPosition: {x: 0, y: 0.2}
  _buttonRadius: 0.8
  _lineWidth: 0.055
  _sortingOrder: 14
  _pressSeed: 44
  _leaveSeed: 56
  _statsHeading: how others chose
  _pressStatLabel: pressed it again
  _leaveStatLabel: left it alone
  _framingLines:
  - Now. This one you have seen before.
  - Not in here. Out there, in the life you had. You stood in front of this exact
    button once, your hand hovering over it, just like now.
  - And you pressed it. [amber]Everything[/amber] after was the long slide down from
    that. The late night, the drink, the headlights, the sudden [red]end[/red] of
    you. All of it, downstream of one little button.
  - I can let you press it again. Change it. Or leave it lying exactly where it is.
    I will not tell you what it does. I never do.
  _pressedReact: You pressed it. Again. You just rolled the dice on your entire existence
    a second time, with no earthly idea what the dice even were. Bold. Idiotic. My
    favourite pairing. Did it change a single thing? I will never, ever say.
  _leftReact: You left it. Naturally you did. You stood at the one button that might
    unpick the whole sorry slide, and you could not make your hand close on it. Too
    frightened of a thing you cannot even name. Did it matter? You will never know.
  _pressLabel: Press it again
  _leaveLabel: Leave it
  _advanceLockout: 0.3
  _buttonFadeIn: 0.45
  _reactHold: 0.4
  _statsFade: 0.5
  _statsHideFade: 0.6
  _buttonFadeOut: 0.4
